    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0322" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.65/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-14T10:00:00+01:00">June 14, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 14—7:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. My telegrams numbers 112, June 9, 7 p.m., and 114, June 12, 7 p.m.<anchor
                        n="14" xml:id="d190-f1"/> Following communiqué published this morning:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Since it has for some time been the desire of the Chief of the Italian
                            Government and of the Chancellor of the Reich to know each other <pb
                                facs="0323" n="223" xml:id="pg223"/> personally and to discuss the
                            general political situation the two statesmen will meet toward the end
                            of the week in a city of northern Italy”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Headlines in the press this morning announce that the meeting will take place
                    today at Villa Pisconi in Stra near Venice.</p>
                <p>This morning’s <hi rendition="#italic">Messaggero</hi> intimates that Mussolini’s
                    chief preoccupation will be to pave the way for Germany’s return to the League
                    of Nations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d190-f1" n="14" xml:id="d190-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed; see telegram No. 129, June 22, 1 p.m., from the Ambassador in
